# Renderers

Renderers owns executable guest implementation: generating bindings from the canonical WIT, building a component without host imports, validating response claims, and testing sandbox failures and native fallback. Registration, command format metadata, paths, and priority remain canonical under <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/extensions">catalog extensions</GuideRef>.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| generate bindings, implement `render`, build a component, and verify its WIT | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers/authoring">Authoring</GuideRef> |
| test compatibility, limits, selection, response validation, and fallback | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers/testing-and-failures">Testing and failures</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Start with a renderer entry registered in the catalog and the exact committed `renderer.wit`. Treat output as presentation only; retain a canonical built-in format for automation and diagnostics.
